# function F(options, flag) { const signal = options.signal; if (signal) { if (flag) first(); listen(signal) } }   F({}, true)
# The call to `listen` follows the inner `if`, so it is in a join block. A join block inherits the guards of its immediate dominator:
# `signal` is never truthy, so neither call runs. With an object in `signal` both run.
